WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.418 --> 00:00:11.418
Is everything going well?

2
00:00:11.418 --> 00:00:15.418
Hallelujah.

3
00:00:15.418 --> 00:00:18.418
Listen.

4
00:00:18.418 --> 00:00:32.418
When you read the Bible, or when you come to church and hear teaching,

5
00:00:32.418 --> 00:00:42.418
or when you try to live your life in a way that makes God happy.

6
00:00:42.418 --> 00:00:49.418
You see this recurring in the Bible, to the glory of the Father.

7
00:00:49.418 --> 00:01:01.418
When you live in such a way, or on the other hand, when you do things that are not good,

8
00:01:02.418 --> 00:01:05.418
then you sin against the Father.

9
00:01:05.418 --> 00:01:08.418
That is one perspective.

10
00:01:08.418 --> 00:01:14.418
But another perspective is, when you live well, or when you sin,

11
00:01:14.418 --> 00:01:22.418
this is also to your advantage, or to the detriment of your life.

12
00:01:22.418 --> 00:01:29.418
So you can always look at faith in two different ways.

13
00:01:29.418 --> 00:01:36.418
To the glory of the Father, or to the benefit of your own life.

14
00:01:36.418 --> 00:01:42.418
And both are one hundred percent true.

15
00:01:42.418 --> 00:01:46.418
They are both completely true.

16
00:01:46.418 --> 00:01:52.418
I just don't like it when I look at a church, or look at teaching,

17
00:01:52.418 --> 00:01:58.418
and I keep hearing from a certain teaching that it is always about yourself.

18
00:01:58.418 --> 00:02:05.418
Do this, and you will be happy, and it is about your emotions, and it is about you, and it is about you, and it is about you.

19
00:02:05.418 --> 00:02:12.418
Eventually, I get tired of that, because I ultimately want to hear that my life is for the glory of the Father.

20
00:02:12.418 --> 00:02:17.418
That is very important, because everything ultimately revolves around the Father.

21
00:02:17.418 --> 00:02:23.418
He made us. He was already there. It is His plan. We live for Him.

22
00:02:23.418 --> 00:02:26.418
So ultimately, everything revolves around Him.

23
00:02:27.418 --> 00:02:29.418
But here is a great lesson.

24
00:02:29.418 --> 00:02:36.418
If you live in such a way that you make the Father smile,

25
00:02:36.418 --> 00:02:41.418
that you live in a way that pleases the Father,

26
00:02:41.418 --> 00:02:43.418
that makes the Father happy,

27
00:02:43.418 --> 00:02:47.418
then that is always to your advantage.

28
00:02:47.418 --> 00:02:52.418
Making God happy is becoming happy yourself.

29
00:02:52.418 --> 00:02:56.418
Not making God happy is becoming unhappy yourself.

30
00:02:56.418 --> 00:02:58.418
That is a guarantee.

31
00:03:00.418 --> 00:03:04.418
Today is about you.

32
00:03:04.418 --> 00:03:08.418
And it makes God the Father very happy.

33
00:03:08.418 --> 00:03:15.418
What we are going to discuss today is one hundred percent your choice.

34
00:03:15.418 --> 00:03:18.418
Your responsibility. It makes you happy.

35
00:03:19.418 --> 00:03:25.418
You, by making the right choices, will lead a wonderful life.

36
00:03:25.418 --> 00:03:32.418
We are going to talk today about being open about relationships in the topic of dating.

37
00:03:32.418 --> 00:03:35.418
Also known as courtship.

38
00:03:35.418 --> 00:03:40.418
So not dating someone once for speed dating and that's it.

39
00:03:40.418 --> 00:03:49.418
I am talking about the period in which you, as a single person in the world,

40
00:03:49.418 --> 00:03:53.418
are going to make a choice for a person.

41
00:03:55.418 --> 00:03:59.418
And this is completely for you.

42
00:03:59.418 --> 00:04:04.418
The choices you are going to make to choose a person,

43
00:04:04.418 --> 00:04:08.418
are indeed life-defining.

44
00:04:10.418 --> 00:04:15.418
Even if you choose to end that relationship.

45
00:04:15.418 --> 00:04:21.418
That relationship still has repercussions for the rest of your life.

46
00:04:23.418 --> 00:04:28.418
Unless you choose to continue with Christ in your life.

47
00:04:28.418 --> 00:04:32.418
Unless you choose to put Christ at the center of your life.

48
00:04:32.418 --> 00:04:39.418
But all the choices you make always have a consequence for your whole, whole life.

49
00:04:40.418 --> 00:04:45.418
And when it comes to the subject of dating,

50
00:04:45.418 --> 00:04:51.418
this is very, very important,

51
00:04:51.418 --> 00:04:56.418
that during that dating period you think of yourself.

52
00:04:56.418 --> 00:04:58.418
Do not think of someone else.

53
00:04:58.418 --> 00:05:04.418
At that moment, you do not have to account to anyone else.

54
00:05:04.418 --> 00:05:09.418
You actually, very crudely said, have nothing to do with anyone.

55
00:05:09.418 --> 00:05:13.418
You are alone. You are wanted by God.

56
00:05:13.418 --> 00:05:17.418
He loves you. I hope you have a relationship with God.

57
00:05:17.418 --> 00:05:21.418
And for the rest, you do not have to account to anyone.

58
00:05:21.418 --> 00:05:24.418
You are wonderfully single.

59
00:05:24.418 --> 00:05:26.418
That is amazing.

60
00:05:26.418 --> 00:05:32.418
And so, and so, when you start dating,

61
00:05:32.418 --> 00:05:35.418
or you are looking for a life partner,

62
00:05:35.418 --> 00:05:40.418
that choice is not to make the other person happy.

63
00:05:40.418 --> 00:05:46.418
That choice is primarily, is this good for me?

64
00:05:46.418 --> 00:05:51.418
Because you were already alone, and you have the choice to remain alone,

65
00:05:51.418 --> 00:05:56.418
or you choose to partner with someone, but that choice is for yourself.

66
00:05:56.418 --> 00:05:59.418
Because it is your life.

67
00:05:59.418 --> 00:06:01.418
God has given you a life.

68
00:06:01.418 --> 00:06:05.418
He has given you the responsibility over your own life.

69
00:06:05.418 --> 00:06:10.418
So who you add to your life is your responsibility.

70
00:06:10.418 --> 00:06:13.418
Do you understand what I mean?

71
00:06:15.418 --> 00:06:17.418
All right.

72
00:06:19.418 --> 00:06:21.418
Hannie.

73
00:06:21.418 --> 00:06:22.418
Okay.

74
00:06:22.418 --> 00:06:27.418
The first question is, why do we date?

75
00:06:28.418 --> 00:06:32.418
And we are talking with you as believers in Jesus,

76
00:06:32.418 --> 00:06:34.418
as followers of Jesus.

77
00:06:38.418 --> 00:06:41.418
Your desire is then to marry.

78
00:06:41.418 --> 00:06:46.418
As Tim said, as a Christian person who follows Jesus Christ,

79
00:06:46.418 --> 00:06:51.418
if you long to be murdered, then date,

80
00:06:51.418 --> 00:06:54.418
the purpose of dating is for clarity.

81
00:06:55.418 --> 00:07:00.418
As Tim also said, if you as a Christian desire to get married,

82
00:07:00.418 --> 00:07:05.418
then the purpose of dating is to gain clarity.

83
00:07:07.418 --> 00:07:09.418
Clarity.

84
00:07:09.418 --> 00:07:12.418
Because of what Tim just said.

85
00:07:16.418 --> 00:07:21.418
Because of the consequences of joining yourself with another person.

86
00:07:25.418 --> 00:07:29.418
In this culture, there are many reasons to date.

87
00:07:29.418 --> 00:07:32.418
And people date just to have fun.

88
00:07:38.418 --> 00:07:41.418
And to simply enjoy being with someone.

89
00:07:47.418 --> 00:07:51.418
But in Christian dating, there is a purpose and an intention.

90
00:07:55.418 --> 00:08:01.418
And that intention is to begin that dating relationship with the goal of marriage.

91
00:08:05.418 --> 00:08:08.418
If that is not your goal yet, then you do not need to date.

92
00:08:10.418 --> 00:08:12.418
It is very simple, very clear.

93
00:08:15.418 --> 00:08:19.418
And we will also talk about singles in two weeks.

94
00:08:25.418 --> 00:08:29.418
Because yes, there is a desire in humanity to marry,

95
00:08:29.418 --> 00:08:32.418
but there can also be a calling on people to remain single.

96
00:08:42.418 --> 00:08:46.418
And there are ways in which married people can glorify God,

97
00:08:46.418 --> 00:08:48.418
in a way that a single cannot.

98
00:08:48.418 --> 00:08:51.418
But there are also ways in which a single can glorify God,

99
00:08:51.418 --> 00:08:53.418
in ways that married people cannot.

100
00:08:55.418 --> 00:08:58.418
And the Bible also says, one is not better than the other,

101
00:08:58.418 --> 00:09:00.418
but you must know your calling.

102
00:09:04.418 --> 00:09:08.418
And you must be content in Christ, no matter what.

103
00:09:14.418 --> 00:09:17.418
So I will say it again, the reason we date as Christians,

104
00:09:17.418 --> 00:09:19.418
is to gain clarity.

105
00:09:19.418 --> 00:09:22.418
In Genesis 1, verses 27 to 28.

106
00:09:32.418 --> 00:09:36.418
God spoke to man as male and female, He made them male and female.

107
00:09:40.418 --> 00:09:43.418
And this is important, for He spoke to both of them.

108
00:09:50.418 --> 00:09:54.418
He declared this word and this purpose over both of them.

109
00:10:03.418 --> 00:10:07.418
He made them as male and female and He commanded them to rule over the earth.

110
00:10:07.418 --> 00:10:09.418
We have talked about this.

111
00:10:11.418 --> 00:10:13.418
They must rule over the earth.

112
00:10:15.418 --> 00:10:17.418
They must build a life with God.

113
00:10:20.418 --> 00:10:23.418
In a lifelong commitment, that is God's purpose.

114
00:10:26.418 --> 00:10:28.418
To raise children.

115
00:10:29.418 --> 00:10:33.418
In Malachi, the Word says that He wants a godly covenant.

116
00:10:39.418 --> 00:10:42.418
So again, if you are looking for a date to become engaged,

117
00:10:42.418 --> 00:10:47.418
then your goal as you build children is to raise them in the way of the Lord.

118
00:10:49.418 --> 00:10:51.418
And if you date with the purpose of getting married later,

119
00:10:51.418 --> 00:10:54.418
then you also want to raise children in the ways of the Lord.

120
00:10:55.418 --> 00:10:57.418
This is the purpose.

121
00:11:00.418 --> 00:11:03.418
And of course to serve Jesus together.

122
00:11:07.418 --> 00:11:09.418
And to serve His purpose in your life.

123
00:11:14.418 --> 00:11:18.418
So when you are dating, you gain clarity about many things.

124
00:11:19.418 --> 00:11:21.418
About the other person.

125
00:11:28.418 --> 00:11:31.418
Can I build a life that will glorify Jesus?

126
00:11:41.418 --> 00:11:45.418
And we said this last year as well, all four of those Sundays,

127
00:11:45.418 --> 00:11:48.418
they are still online on YouTube, you can watch them back.

128
00:11:49.418 --> 00:11:50.418
That was good.

129
00:11:52.418 --> 00:11:54.418
And we repeat a lot of things.

130
00:11:54.418 --> 00:11:56.418
Because it doesn't change.

131
00:12:02.418 --> 00:12:05.418
So you gain a lot of clarity about the other person when you date.

132
00:12:08.418 --> 00:12:10.418
The point is this.

133
00:12:10.418 --> 00:12:15.418
God has a purpose for your life.

134
00:12:16.418 --> 00:12:20.418
And if you are single, you are pursuing God.

135
00:12:21.418 --> 00:12:22.418
And you have a purpose.

136
00:12:23.418 --> 00:12:28.418
And one of the most wonderful things you can discover in life,

137
00:12:28.418 --> 00:12:30.418
is why you are alive.

138
00:12:31.418 --> 00:12:34.418
That is one of the most wonderful things you can discover.

139
00:12:35.418 --> 00:12:36.418
This is my calling.

140
00:12:37.418 --> 00:12:38.418
This is what I live for.

141
00:12:40.418 --> 00:12:43.418
And maybe you are thinking to yourself, wait a minute, I don't know what I live for.

142
00:12:43.418 --> 00:12:49.418
Well, the very first thing you live for, and even if you were to vocalize that,

143
00:12:49.418 --> 00:12:53.418
your first calling is to say, I live for Jesus.

144
00:12:54.418 --> 00:12:58.418
So even if you don't know, maybe you are called by God to go into politics,

145
00:12:58.418 --> 00:13:00.418
and you still don't know that you should go into politics.

146
00:13:00.418 --> 00:13:01.418
That can be.

147
00:13:01.418 --> 00:13:05.418
But what you can already know is that you live to glorify God.

148
00:13:06.418 --> 00:13:10.418
So if it starts with that, then you are already doing very well.

149
00:13:10.418 --> 00:13:11.418
Yes.

150
00:13:11.418 --> 00:13:12.418
May I say that?

151
00:13:12.418 --> 00:13:13.418
Certainly.

152
00:13:13.418 --> 00:13:16.418
You should already have clarity about yourself before you start dating.

153
00:13:16.418 --> 00:13:17.418
That is the point.

154
00:13:17.418 --> 00:13:20.418
You should have clarity about yourself before you begin a relationship.

155
00:13:20.418 --> 00:13:25.418
If you do not yet know who you are in Christ, then you should not start dating.

156
00:13:25.418 --> 00:13:31.418
For you must find yourself in who you are before you gain clarity about someone else.

157
00:13:31.418 --> 00:13:32.418
That is it.

158
00:13:32.418 --> 00:13:36.418
If you do not yet know who you are in Christ, then it is not yet time to start dating.

159
00:13:37.418 --> 00:13:41.418
For you must first be established, rooted in your identity in Christ,

160
00:13:41.418 --> 00:13:44.418
before you can gain clarity about someone else.

161
00:13:44.418 --> 00:13:51.418
So when you see Mientje walking by and you think,

162
00:13:51.418 --> 00:13:53.418
hey, she has beautiful eyebrows.

163
00:13:53.418 --> 00:14:03.418
If you think that, the most important question to that person is, who are you?

164
00:14:03.418 --> 00:14:10.418
And we live in a society and therefore, what we just did,

165
00:14:10.418 --> 00:14:12.418
this is holy ground.

166
00:14:12.418 --> 00:14:15.418
And the moment I felt the Holy Spirit say,

167
00:14:15.418 --> 00:14:18.418
this is not a trivial staff what we are doing here.

168
00:14:18.418 --> 00:14:25.418
We live in a society where this world is pushing younger people,

169
00:14:25.418 --> 00:14:28.418
especially, I'm talking to you now, younger people,

170
00:14:28.418 --> 00:14:33.418
we live in a society that is absolutely aimless for many people.

171
00:14:33.418 --> 00:14:34.418
And that is it.

172
00:14:34.418 --> 00:14:35.418
And that is it.

173
00:14:35.418 --> 00:14:36.418
And that is it.

174
00:14:36.418 --> 00:14:37.418
And that is it.

175
00:14:37.418 --> 00:14:38.418
And that is it.

176
00:14:38.418 --> 00:14:39.418
And that is it.

177
00:14:39.418 --> 00:14:40.418
And that is it.

178
00:14:40.418 --> 00:14:41.418
And that is it.

179
00:14:41.418 --> 00:14:42.418
And that is it.

180
00:15:12.418 --> 00:15:13.418
The value is not it.

181
00:15:13.418 --> 00:15:14.418
I don't know.

182
00:15:14.418 --> 00:15:15.418
I give up.

183
00:15:15.418 --> 00:15:16.418
I give up.

184
00:15:16.418 --> 00:15:18.418
Yes, but what do you want then?

185
00:15:18.418 --> 00:15:19.418
I don't know.

186
00:15:19.418 --> 00:15:22.418
Passivity is of today.

187
00:15:22.418 --> 00:15:27.418
And the last thing you can use, young lady or young man,

188
00:15:27.418 --> 00:15:31.418
or middle-aged lady, or middle-aged man,

189
00:15:31.418 --> 00:15:34.418
or older lady, or older man, who cares?

190
00:15:34.418 --> 00:15:39.418
The last thing you can use is a passive partner in life.

191
00:15:39.418 --> 00:15:43.418
You won't achieve anything with that.

192
00:15:43.418 --> 00:15:50.418
And this is why I just said, this teaching is about you.

193
00:15:50.418 --> 00:15:54.418
Here you can talk about dating and about relationships and about choosing a partner,

194
00:15:54.418 --> 00:15:56.418
you can be very selfish about it.

195
00:15:56.418 --> 00:15:58.418
This is all about you.

196
00:15:58.418 --> 00:16:04.418
Because suppose you think to yourself, my calling is to make the Lord happy.

197
00:16:04.418 --> 00:16:07.418
And you see someone passing by in life,

198
00:16:07.418 --> 00:16:10.418
and you really like them and they have nice talks and this and that.

199
00:16:10.418 --> 00:16:18.418
But for the rest, their entire worldview and their vision to honor God is nonsense.

200
00:16:18.418 --> 00:16:30.418
Why would you put your own worldview on hold for Mr. Drifter?

201
00:16:30.418 --> 00:16:33.418
But seriously.

202
00:16:33.418 --> 00:16:35.418
Seriously.

203
00:16:35.418 --> 00:16:38.418
And this is very important.

204
00:16:38.418 --> 00:16:44.418
Because Mr. vagabond will ultimately bring you down as well.

205
00:16:44.418 --> 00:16:49.418
Because really, oh my gosh, church listen carefully.

206
00:16:49.418 --> 00:16:58.418
The number of relationships that fall apart because one of the two has no life vision,

207
00:16:58.418 --> 00:17:07.418
or has no vision of God, that number is higher than the number that is doing well.

208
00:17:07.418 --> 00:17:13.418
In the Netherlands and in Belgium and in America and in Australia, the Western world,

209
00:17:13.418 --> 00:17:18.418
more relationships are breaking apart than are staying together.

210
00:17:18.418 --> 00:17:28.418
And I know, I know as a fact, a couple in Christ is a couple that stands firm.

211
00:17:28.418 --> 00:17:31.418
That is really true.

212
00:17:31.418 --> 00:17:37.418
And I have sometimes provided pastoral guidance towards marriage with people

213
00:17:37.418 --> 00:17:42.418
and then I always say, you should look at that couple, look at that couple,

214
00:17:42.418 --> 00:17:45.418
look at that couple, look at that couple, look at that couple.

215
00:17:45.418 --> 00:17:49.418
And then I always point to the couples that I respect,

216
00:17:49.418 --> 00:17:52.418
that those people have lived their lives in Christ.

217
00:17:53.418 --> 00:17:59.418
And so the most important thing is that you as a single person look at that other person.

218
00:17:59.418 --> 00:18:04.418
Question 1, does that other person have faith in Jesus?

219
00:18:04.418 --> 00:18:10.418
Question 2, does that person have a vision for his or her life?

220
00:18:16.418 --> 00:18:20.418
We go to 2 Corinthians 6 and it is about a yoke.

221
00:18:32.418 --> 00:18:35.418
And this context is not specifically about marriage,

222
00:18:35.418 --> 00:18:39.418
but just about all relationships to which you can apply this

223
00:18:39.418 --> 00:18:41.418
and among those, marriage is very important.

224
00:18:46.418 --> 00:18:49.418
Do not be unequally yoked with unbelievers.

225
00:18:53.418 --> 00:18:57.418
So again, Paul assumes he is speaking to a follower of Christ.

226
00:19:01.418 --> 00:19:05.418
And I do the same, I assume that you are following Jesus with all your heart and strength.

227
00:19:05.418 --> 00:19:07.418
So this is for you, this is for us.

228
00:19:13.418 --> 00:19:17.418
For what is the relationship between righteousness and lawlessness?

229
00:19:22.418 --> 00:19:24.418
And what does light have to do with darkness?

230
00:19:27.418 --> 00:19:29.418
This is that two-edged sword.

231
00:19:35.418 --> 00:19:38.418
This could not be clearer or sharper.

232
00:19:40.418 --> 00:19:42.418
I love it when God is really clear.

233
00:19:46.418 --> 00:19:50.418
You should thank God that He has given you a verse like that.

234
00:19:59.418 --> 00:20:04.418
For if we understand that God gives us these instructions for our protection and for our best interest.

235
00:20:06.418 --> 00:20:09.418
And that He is not trying to make your life difficult.

236
00:20:14.418 --> 00:20:17.418
For you might think, yes, now I have very few people over God.

237
00:20:21.418 --> 00:20:23.418
There are so many people out there and so few here.

238
00:20:25.418 --> 00:20:26.418
And that is true.

239
00:20:28.418 --> 00:20:29.418
But you also need to be selective.

240
00:20:31.418 --> 00:20:33.418
For all the reasons that Tim just mentioned.

241
00:20:36.418 --> 00:20:39.418
For you do not want to unite your light with darkness.

242
00:20:42.418 --> 00:20:46.418
You do not want to partner yourself with someone who is unequal.

243
00:20:49.418 --> 00:20:50.418
Then you cannot walk together.

244
00:20:57.418 --> 00:21:03.418
The yoke, the yoke, that was a beam that rested on the shoulders of two oxen so that they could carry a weight together.

245
00:21:06.418 --> 00:21:12.418
You cannot bear the weight and goals of life if you walk in an unequal commitment to Jesus Christ.

246
00:21:26.418 --> 00:21:28.418
How many of you know that life brings weight with it?

247
00:21:36.418 --> 00:21:42.418
Whether you are single or married, there is weight in life and you must bear it, and that is why it is important to have an equal yoke.

248
00:21:57.418 --> 00:22:01.418
